t_coverage":0.5,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":1.2136842869326945,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":61.9,"_gate_accruals":-0.11460040461152787,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":74.7,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.5109429154675541,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.016324819736960188,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":-0.005495299103942267,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":355.34871142160716,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.06248187622284008,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":37.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.030278256027939904,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":43.4,"_gate_pool_share":-0.21925177162868725,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11300939367180285,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":81.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.2835211906362525,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.011926531443106547,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":61.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10192965856307648,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.022630352989557734,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":78.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07915904357175207,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01332,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Pacira BioSciences, Inc. engages in the development, manufacture, marketing, distribution, and sale of non-opioid pain management and regenerative health solutions to healthcare practitioners in the United States. The company offers EXPAREL, a bupivacaine liposome injectable suspension for postsurgical pain management; ZILRETTA, a triamcinolone acetonide extended-release injectable suspension indicated for the management of osteoarthritis and knee pain; and iovera system, a non-opioid handheld cryoanalgesia device used to deliver controlled doses of cold temperature to targeted nerves to produce neurolytic block that interrupts the pain-transmitting signals of a peripheral nerve. It also develops PCRX-201, a novel gene therapy vector platform enabling local administration of genetic medicines with the potential to treat large prevalent diseases like osteoarthritis. It has a development and commercialization, and supply agreement with Aratana Therapeutics, Inc. for NOCITA, a bupivacaine liposome injectable suspension product for use in animals. The company was formerly known as Pacira Pharmaceuticals, Inc. and changed its name to Pacira BioSciences, Inc. in April 2019. Pacira BioSciences, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frank D. Lee | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 825 people. Revenue per employee of $880K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 32%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $166K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $70K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Pacira BioSciences, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.5B market cap on $726M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +19.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $137M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 21.61\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9216564073866815},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of PCRX and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/22/Behavioral_Patterns_of_PCRX_and_Institutional_Flows_111226112201_1794543721.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794543721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are BWIN, CCC, PCRX Obtaining Fair Deals for their Shareholders?","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/are-bwin-ccc-pcrx-obtaining-fair-deals-for-their-shareholders-302936701.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794422580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Pacira BioSciences (PCRX) After Earnings Surprise Is The Stock Already Fully Valued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharma